-- ============================================================================
-- 22_inner_tile_loop_descriptor.surql
-- 2026-06-14 — EXACT decode of the INNER TILE LOOP inside loc_8c0344d4 and the
-- nature/origin of the descriptor table at 0x8C1F9F9C. Sourced ENTIRELY from
-- marvelous2 build/bank03.asm (loc_8c0344d4 inner loop loc_8c03478e..loc_8c034864;
-- list-init/builder loc_8c0337bc literal pool loc_8c0338a8).
-- Apply AFTER 17_tiling_geometry_validated.surql, then 07_dedup_edges.surql.
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor SET date='2026-06-14', confidence='high', status='confirmed',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  note='INNER TILE LOOP of the body walker loc_8c0344d4 (bank03.asm). The OUTER loop (loc_8c0345c4) iterates the GFX2 cell 8-byte records (sel @ r11+6). Per record it sets the per-record TILE COUNT = u8(@(0x1,r13)) + 1 (bank03:10357-10361 mov.b @(0x1,r13),r0; add 0x01,r0; stored stack@0x4) and seeds the per-tile descriptor cursor r13. The INNER loop body is loc_8c03478e..loc_8c034864 with back-edge at bank03:10757-10760 (cmp/ge stack@0x4 ; bf.s loc_8c03478e ; add 0x04,r13 — i.e. r13 advances +4 bytes PER TILE). Each tile reads a 4-byte descriptor record at r13: byte[0]=r5 (a per-tile MULTIPLIER/base, also = the m-extent fed to submit via mov.b @r13 at 10516/10558), byte[1]=tile count-base (read once per RECORD at +0x1), byte[2]=X step factor, byte[3]=Y step factor. The per-tile STEP is COMPUTED, not an explicit (dx,dy): bank03:10617-10639 r5=u8(@r13); xstep_raw = r5*u8(@(0x2,r13)) - stack@0x24 ; ystep_raw = r5*u8(@(0x3,r13)) - stack@0x20 ; then facing/flip sign (loc_8c0347bc: if XMIR(stack@0x60 & r9=0x10) neg ystep; if YMIR(&r8=0x20) neg xstep-equivalent) ; then scaled by node+0xEC/+0xF0 (fr12/fr13 = step*scaleX/scaleY at 10661-10668) and ADDED to the cumulative pen written to stack r15+0x30/0x34 (10673-10683). So a tiled cell renders the SAME GFX1 sel REPEATED at COUNT stepped anchors forming a regular 1D chain OR 2D grid (the grid shape is encoded by the byte[2]/byte[3] step factors and the stack@0x20/0x24 row/col accumulators muls.w at 10623/10629), confirming finding:tiling_grid_is_engine_correct. NOTE the X/Y mirror flags here are the RECORD flags r11+4 (0x4000 X / 0x8000 Y) tested at 10475-10477 / 10500-10503, distinct from facing pen-negation (neg r10) done at record entry loc_8c034548.';

-- The descriptor table is RUNTIME-BUILT per FRAME, NOT a static ROM/DAT table.
UPSERT finding:descriptor_table_runtime_built SET date='2026-06-14', confidence='high', status='confirmed',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  note='The tile descriptor table at 0x8C1F9F9C is RUNTIME-BUILT PER FRAME, NOT static and NOT rippable from the DAT. PROOF (bank03.asm): (1) 0x8C1F9F9C lies ABOVE the entire loaded code/data image — bank1c ends at 0x8c1c9d98 (build/bank1c.asm EndofFile), and 0x8c1f9f9c is in the uninitialized RAM gap between end-of-code and the char-struct page 0x8c268340, so it is BSS scratch, not a ROM section. (2) The per-frame render-list initializer loc_8c0337bc (literal pool loc_8c0338a8) RESETS this subsystem each render pass: it stores the TA write cursor 0x8c1f9d88<-0, the descriptor base 0x8c1f9f9c into the cursor 0x8c1f9d98, then at bank03:8265-8269 calls bank12 builder loc_8c129728 with r14=0x0CE60000 (the part-pixel decode buffer Texture_Decompress_Buffer), r5=0, r6=0x0C00 (3072 = the table BYTE size; next allocation 0x8c1fab9c = 0x8c1f9f9c+0xC00 => 768 entries x 4 bytes). (3) The table is the ONLY consumer of 0x8C1F9F9C, indexed by node[+0xDC]<<2 (walker seeds r13 = 0x8c1f9f9c + (node+0xDC<<2) at bank03:10247-10253; sibling scale-walker loc_8c0348c8 uses the same +0xDC<<2 pattern). node[+0xDC] is the per-object GLOBAL tile cursor into this frame-local table. CONCLUSION: tiling cannot be derived purely from PLxx_DAT offline because the (count + step factors) are emitted into 0x8C1F9F9C at frame time by loc_8c129728 from the decoded-part buffer at 0x0CE60000. HOWEVER finding:tiling_geometry_byte_faithful already shows render_frame.c reproduces the per-tile m-extent EXACTLY by reading this same table at (node+0xDC + k)*4 — so the count+step ARE captured, just at RUNTIME, via the descriptor cursor not the DAT.';

-- The clean Oracle recipe (descriptor-direct, no position clustering).
UPSERT finding:tile_descriptor_oracle_recipe SET date='2026-06-14', confidence='high', status='confirmed',
  note='CLEAN per-(sid,record) tiling capture WITHOUT position-clustering: read the descriptor bytes at r13 directly. ASMTRACE already hooks PC 0x8C034864 (per-tile convergence) and already exports the r13 column (= 0x8C1F9F9C + offset, the per-TILE descriptor cursor) plus accX/accY. At PC 0x8C034864 the engine has, per emitted tile: r13 = current tile descriptor ptr; read_u8(r13+0)=base/m, read_u8(r13+1)=record tile-count-base, read_u8(r13+2)=Xstep factor, read_u8(r13+3)=Ystep factor; r11 = current record ptr (record_index = (r11 - cell_record0)/8; sel=read_u16(r11+6); flags=read_u16(r11+4)); accX/accY = cumulative pen AFTER this tile. RECIPE: one ASMTRACE frame on a NEUTRAL-pose (facing-0) Ryu, augment the hook to also emit the 4 descriptor bytes u8[r13..r13+3] per line. Group lines by sel/record_index; tile COUNT = u8(r13+1)+1 (constant within a record); per-tile (dx,dy) NATIVE offsets = the stepped accX/accY deltas with facing pen-negation undone (dx_native = -accX for facing path; the engine negates X pen on facing via neg r10 at loc_8c034548, and the per-tile step X-component flips sign under record XMIR flag 0x4000 — so capture at facing-0 with no mirror to get the canonical grid). This is unambiguous: the descriptor bytes give count+step factors DIRECTLY; no dedup/clustering needed.';

-- Facing answer.
UPSERT finding:tile_facing_effect SET date='2026-06-14', confidence='high', status='confirmed',
  note='FACING vs the tile grid (bank03.asm loc_8c0344d4). Facing affects TWO things, both sign-flips, NOT the descriptor step factors themselves: (1) the PEN ORIGIN x is negated at record entry loc_8c034548 (neg r10,r10 when facing nonzero), and (2) the per-tile X step contribution is sign-conditioned by the RECORD mirror flags (XMIR 0x4000 tested at loc_8c0346c4-region toggles which axis negates; loc_8c0347bc neg r5/r4 on the 0x10/0x20 PCW mirror bits). The descriptor byte[2]/byte[3] STEP FACTORS are facing-INVARIANT magnitudes; facing/mirror only chooses their sign. CONSEQUENCE for the editor: capture/derive the grid at facing-0 (no pen negation, no XMIR) and you get the canonical native (dx,dy). To render the opposite facing, negate the X component of every tile offset AND the pen origin. The facing-0 offsets are the static per-(sid,record) grid; flips are derivable.';

-- Static-per-pose answer.
UPSERT finding:tile_grid_is_per_pose_static SET date='2026-06-14', confidence='high', status='confirmed',
  note='IS THE TILE GRID STABLE PER (sid,record)? The COUNT and the STEP FACTORS (descriptor bytes 1,2,3) are a property of the (sprite_id, record_index) pose — they are emitted by loc_8c129728 from the decoded part geometry, NOT from live pos/zoom. What live state contributes is ONLY: facing/mirror SIGN (see finding:tile_facing_effect) and the SCALE multiply by node+0xEC/+0xF0 (loc_8c03478e fr12/fr13 = step*scale, bank03:10661-10668) which uniformly scales the whole grid. So the NATIVE (pre-scale, facing-0) per-tile (dx,dy) IS a static per-(sid,record) property and is bakeable, exactly as finding:tiling_geometry_byte_faithful proved render_frame reproduces it byte-faithful. Position/zoom do NOT change the grid shape or count — they only scale+translate the whole assembled part. So baking PLxx_tiles.json={sid:{record_index:[(dx,dy)...]}} at facing-0/scale-1 is valid; multiply by scale and sign-flip for facing at render time.';

-- edges
RELATE finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor->cites->routine:loc_8c0344d4 SET kind='cites';
RELATE finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor->about->finding:body_walker_tiling SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:descriptor_table_runtime_built->cites->routine:loc_8c0344d4 SET kind='cites';
RELATE finding:descriptor_table_runtime_built->about->finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tile_descriptor_oracle_recipe->about->finding:descriptor_table_runtime_built SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tile_facing_effect->about->finding:inner_tile_loop_descriptor SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tile_grid_is_per_pose_static->about->finding:tiling_geometry_byte_faithful SET kind='about';
